    <string name="pin_guide_title">Keep kid mode locked in</string>
    <string name="pin_guide_intro">Kid mode pins the app to the screen. Do this once so only a grown-up can unpin it:</string>
    <string name="pin_guide_step1">Open Settings, then Security and privacy, then More security settings, then Pin windows. (On other tablets, look for Screen pinning.)</string>
    <string name="pin_guide_step2">Turn it on, and turn on Ask for PIN before unpinning.</string>
    <string name="pin_guide_step3">Come back and start kid mode. Android will ask you to confirm; tap Start.</string>
    <string name="pin_guide_step4">Leaving kid mode: hold the grown-up button, then unlock your tablet.</string>
    <string name="pin_guide_step5">Also turn off Smart Lock (Extend Unlock, trusted places and devices) in the lock screen settings. Otherwise the lock screen can be swiped away and a child could get out.</string>
